From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] zink: no disk cache on iOS

Zink's disk cache keeps its pipeline caches and, through
get_disk_shader_cache, the GLSL frontend's. A cache reused across
launches on KosmicKrisp has not been checked yet (prior work with Zink
on KosmicKrisp saw stale pipelines), so on iOS Zink makes none.
KosmicKrisp's own cache of the pipelines Zink creates (0015) is
unaffected.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-mesa-gl-ios-build.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
index b232cd5..9340695 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -317,7 +317,11 @@ disk_cache_init(struct zink_screen *screen)
    if (zink_debug & ZINK_DEBUG_SHADERDB)
       return true;
 
-#ifdef ENABLE_SHADER_CACHE
+   /* On iOS Zink keeps no disk cache (nor, through it, the GLSL cache) until
+    * reusing one across launches is checked on KosmicKrisp; KosmicKrisp's own
+    * cache of the pipelines Zink creates is unaffected.
+    */
+#if defined(ENABLE_SHADER_CACHE) && !(DETECT_OS_APPLE && TARGET_OS_IPHONE)
    struct mesa_blake3 ctx;
    _mesa_blake3_init(&ctx);
 
-- 
